<figure class="sample-review" aria-labelledby="sample-review-title">
  <figcaption>Illustrative example. Not a client project.</figcaption>
  <div class="sample-review-body">
    <p class="review-topic">Website enquiry form</p>
    <h2 id="sample-review-title">Is the quote request too hard to find?</h2>
    <dl class="review-observations">
      <div>
        <dt>Example issue</dt>
        <dd>
          The quote link is only in the footer. The form asks for a full address before explaining
          which areas the business covers.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>Recommended change</dt>
        <dd>
          Put a quote link beside the service description. Ask for a postcode first, with the full
          address later if needed.
        </dd>
      </div>
      <div>
        <dt>What to check</dt>
        <dd>
          Test on a phone, confirm messages arrive and compare completed requests where reliable
          figures are available.
        </dd>
      </div>
    </dl>
  </div>
  <p class="sample-review-caption">
    An example of the reasoning behind a recommendation, not a claim about client results.
  </p>
</figure>
